{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8xOTk5LS1CZWZvcmUvRnJhbmslMjBBbmQlMjBPbGxpZSUyMCUyODE5OTUlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Frank And Ollie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/eUIELE2IkuWkAc3JzjYz6J2Lpx5.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/pmvWLzvPYEvzD08tKRBn4g4SWLq.jpg","description":"Before computer graphics, special effects wizardry, and out-of-this world technology, the magic of animation flowed from the pencils of two of the greatest animators The Walt Disney Company ever produced -- Frank Thomas and Ollie Johnston. Frank and Ollie, the talent behind BAMBI, PINOCCHIO, LADY AND THE TRAMP, THE JUNGLE BOOK, and others, set the standard for such modern-day hits as THE LION KING. It was their creative genius that helped make Disney synonymous with brilliant animation, magnificent music, and emotional storytelling. Take a journey with these extraordinary artists as they share secrets, insights, and the inspiration behind some of the greatest animated movies the world has ever known!\n\nRated PG · Released 20 Oct 1995 · United States of America · Language: English · 89 min\nStudio: Theodore Thomas Productions, Walt Disney Pictures\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"1995","genres":["Documentary","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"7.4","runtime":"89 min","cast":["Frank Thomas","Ollie Johnston","Glen Keane","Andrew Gaskill","John Canemaker","John Culhane"],"director":["Theodore Thomas"],"released":"1995-10-20T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"Their friendship changed the face of animation.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Theodore Thomas","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/7PzxpqCvBfKaZg3PgoZWjJkk0eb.jpg"},{"name":"Frank Thomas","character":"Himself","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/ex3jyUogtwMt2zQgzmh3cwEz8ds.jpg"},{"name":"Ollie Johnston","character":"Himself","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/7LShcoYbJg7vfXV2lSjzTlGAGb.jpg"},{"name":"Glen Keane","character":"Him